    "lawCode": "Amd §404-ee, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S790A\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to waiving\ncertain fees for distinctive \"September eleventh, two thousand one\nremembrance\" license plates for certain first responders\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would allow for the waiving of fees for the distinctive\n\"September eleventh, two thousand one remembrance\" license plates for\ncertified first responders who are disabled, or their spouses as a\nresult of a certified World Trade Center medical condition.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:  Section one of this bill adds a new subdivi-\nsion 4 to section 401-ee of the vehicle and traffic law by adding\nlanguage to allow fees prescribed for the issuance and renewal of a\nlicense note to a person who sustained a permanent disability as a\nresult of their participation in the rescue effort on 9/11, or their\nspouse to be waived.\n\nSection two of this bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nEach day, the number of deaths for first responders who Participated in\nWorld Trade Center rescue, recovery and cleanup, operations continues to\ngrow. Almost eighteen years after the attacks on the World. Trade\nCenter, over ten thousand first responders and others in the disaster\narea have been diagnosed with cancer and other debilitating illnesses,\nand more than 2,000 deaths have been related to 9/11 related illness.\n\nEven for first responders who are still in good health, the fear of\nfuture illness is constantly in their minds. However, these heroes still\nhave to focus on providing. financially for their families, and prepar-\ning for the potential risk of developing illness as a result of their\ncall to serve on that fateful day. For their sacrifife, these individ-\nuals and their spouses deserve the remembrance plate honoring their\nheroism without the additional cost charged for these plates.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS. 5845 of 2019/20; Advanced to Third Reading Calendar\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effort on the 60th day.\n",
